    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d34">

                <pb facs="0163" n="64" sameAs="frus:frus1936v02/pg64"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860F.5151/87: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Czechoslovakia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Wright</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Prague</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-12-24T13:00:00+01:00">December 24, 1936—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 24—11:10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>62. I am today in receipt through the Foreign Office of a written statement of
                    the National Bank declaring that it now allots and in future will allot exchange
                    for all American goods strictly in accordance <pb facs="0164" n="65"
                        xml:id="pg65"/> with the provisions of section 2 of supplemental agreement
                    of March 29, 1935.</p>
                <p>Text of covering note and of foreign statement by mail.<anchor n="31"
                        xml:id="d34-f1"/> Written confirmation of such other points as have been
                    satisfactorily resolved to date as reported in my despatches is promised early
                    in January.<anchor n="32" xml:id="d34-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wright</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
